# Netlify serves the repository root as-is: the project has no build command and
# an empty publish directory. That means every file in the folder is a public
# URL unless it is listed here.
#
# firebase.json has an equivalent "hosting.ignore" list, but Netlify does not
# read firebase.json, so that list was doing nothing. Without this file,
# /firebase/database.rules.json and /package.json are downloadable from the
# live site.

# Firebase config and emulator internals
firebase/**
.firebaserc
firebase.json

# Build and test tooling, not part of the site
scripts/**
tests/**
node_modules/**
.firebase/**
package.json
package-lock.json
playwright.config.js

# Repo metadata
.git/**
.github/**
.gitignore
.netlifyignore
README.md

# No page links to it; terms-and-conditions.html is the published version
*.docx

*.log
